# The REPLACE hit box.
#
# A REPLACE takes the target's records out of the frame and puts the
# replacement's in their place, so whatever of the target's box the
# replacement does not cover answers nothing at all -- the native op is gone
# and the control is not there. On the shipped camera that was a dead ring
# 1,497 pixels wide around a 20x16 icon in a 79x23 Report button, proven on
# classic548 and on the CS1 live lane: a right-click 7px left of the icon's
# ink offered Cancel and nothing else, and a left-click took no screenshot.
#
# Porcelain now stands a second owned node the size of the TARGET under the
# picture and arms the item's op on that. It is what these lines are. It draws
# nothing -- scene=0, so the emit walk drops it -- and the report button's
# pixels are byte-identical before and after on both lanes (a 120x33 crop at
# 440,470 on classic548 and a 120x35 crop at 400,468 on cs1live: 0 differing
# pixels of 3,960 and of 4,200).
#
# stone601 states nothing here on purpose: the touch frame presents no report
# button, the camera falls back to a viewport corner, and a corner ornament is
# not a REPLACE -- so that lane has no hit box to declare and passes unaltered.
#
# A reason is ONE line. The parser splits every line on its own ` = `, so a
# wrapped continuation is read as a second declaration with no reason and the
# whole file is refused.

owned-add camera_report~hit = the hit box a REPLACE owes the box it consumed: invisible (scene=0), carrying the item's op, so the whole Report button answers again

only-after BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=454,480 79x23 = the same node said as a box, on the two fixed frames, whose report button's own box this is
only-after BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=437,480 79x23 = the same node on the native and resizable toplevels, where the report button sits 17px further left
only-after BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=408,467 100x32 = the same node on the CS1 lane, where the 2004 report pill is 100x32
